{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes","id":992054,"title":"CofD cosmology idea: linked universes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T15:19:07-07:00","id":992054,"title":"CofD cosmology idea: linked universes","content":"I recently came up with an idea for reconciling the &quot;crowded&quot; nature of the ChroD setting, that I really kind of like. Each line (plus Blue Book) represents a variation of a central universe, each close enough that the differences are not readily apparent and travel between them is possible. Some of the universes are closer than others- for example, the vampire and werewolf universes are close enough to be nearly linked. They aren't even so much different universes as different layers of reality in which the same places and people can exist simultaneously. As an example, a vampire out on a walk might experience a shift in Phase without noticing it, and might spend part of that walk in the Geist universe. <br /> <br /> However, they would eventually exist and slip back into their own unless they encountered a phenomenon native to the Geist universe and had a significant enough encounter to anchor them in that universe, thus causing the same person to simultaneously exist in both universes. <br /> <br /> Each universe has a Supernatural Primacy, a dominant supernatural paradigm. Werewolf has its spirit cosmology, Mage has the Supernal, Demon has the Machine, and so on. Just because these phenomena are native to one universe doesn't mean that they can't effect others. If a being from one universe contacts another and begins to exist in it as well, they still retain their connection to their native supernatural paradigm. So Contracts work in the Mage world, and so on. <br /> <br /> The most powerful beings of each world (extremely powerful spirits, archmasters, Gentry, the Machine) and so on are aware of the other universes, and can interact with them to a limited extent. However, they're usually interested in keeping the boundaries at least somewhat coherent. The Exarchs, for example, have tried to take control of the Machine, but found it impossible, and now mostly try to leave it alone and settle for letting it do what it does, since they at least have roughly similar short term goals. The various extremely powerful entities glimpsed in the &quot;blue book&quot; universe are in fact beings from these other universes reaching into it. For example, the Gentry can take someone from any of the universes, but find it easiest to take from the Changeling one. Mages and Demons tend to be the most likely to notice these patterns, being the most likely to investigate reality sharts, but most of them know better than to mess with them and try to pin things down, as this tends to have unintended consequences. For example, no one's been able to find the Zeka after that business with the two Arcadias.<br /> <br /> Crossover theories have a place here too. They form like mangrove roots, holding the universes together but separate. Without them, the worlds would collide and melt into nothing or drift too far apart. <br /> <br /> Hunter, Deviant, and Beast do not have their own universes. Instead, Hunters and Beasts are the result of someone from the &quot;base&quot; blue book universe being sucked into one or more of the other universes. Deviant takes place by default in the Blue Book universes, but it's entirely possible for Deviants to end up in any or multiple of the other universes. <br /> <br /> In the spaces between the universes are countless alternate timelines and half-formed universes. Various powerful entities find this space to be a useful place to stuff their various projects, including the alternate timelines the Machine experiments with. Assorted True Fae, archmasters, Incarnae, and so on have also noticed that there seems to be something very large some ways behind their cluster, something which looks sort of similar and is sometimes going through an apocalypse and sometimes isn't. They have collectively resolved to leave this thing alone. <br /> <br /> They've caught glimpses of other clusters father off in the distance, too. Supposedly an archmaster tried to communicate with one of the closer ones, and received a handwritten note, which simply read: &quot;Fuck off. - The I.C.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-23-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:27:48-07:00","id":992059,"title":"","content":"It reminds me a thought experiment I once toyed with, which was based around giving every gameline its own &quot;sub space&quot; in which reality operates under different laws and contains different phenomena. You can find it in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/26755-nations-in-the-dark-shard-brainstorming-thread\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:40:02-07:00","id":992071,"title":"","content":"Interesting! Mind if I steal the basic naming scheme?<br /> <br /> So, here's how it's set up, with nine worlds:: <br /> <br /> The World of Darkness<br /> <br /> The World of Blood<br /> <br /> The World of Spirits<br /> <br /> The World of Mana<br /> <br /> The World of Thorns<br /> <br /> The World of Fire<br /> <br /> The World of Ghosts<br /> <br /> The World of Pillars<br /> <br /> The World of Gears","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:49:47-07:00","id":992077,"title":"","content":"Various archmasters have signed a petition for the Gentry to change their realm's name, as every year at least one Mage accidentally erases themself from existence trying to establish a solid connection between them. &quot;It's just way too confusing. Come on, guys, help us out here.&quot; - Galaculex the Destroyer, archmaster. <br /> <br /> Does anyone know how to say &quot;and then a skeleton jumped out&quot; in Latin? I like the idea that various sages have come up with that as the one iron law of the cosmos. Everything ultimately trends towards maximum spookiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:06:51-07:00","id":992083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992077#post992077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Various archmasters have signed a petition for the Gentry to change their realm's name, as every year at least one Mage accidentally erases themself from existence trying to establish a solid connection between them. &quot;It's just way too confusing. Come on, guys, help us out here.&quot; - Galaculex the Destroyer, archmaster.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know how to say &quot;and then a skeleton jumped out&quot; in Latin? I like the idea that various sages have come up with that as the one iron law of the cosmos. Everything ultimately trends towards maximum spookiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they'd say something like &quot;Et ecce, terror emergit!&quot; (&quot;And lo, fear emerges!&quot;). It sounds a tinge less silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:36:33-07:00","id":992102,"title":"","content":"I've always kind of assumed something similar. I posited a similar theory about the Marvel and DC comic universes (in terms of the books in each universe, not the two universes coexisting together).<br /> <br /> That said, I generally look at them less as distinct universes and more as vibrational frequencies that frequently overlap. Hunter and Beast maintain pitches centered right in the middle and see the most overlapping fluctuations with the other lines. And the localized nature of the ChroD books and the general lack of global conspiracies means that most of the times these groups can do their own thing without ever encountering another type of entity. But when a vampire encounters a werewolf or a hunter runs into something that's not quite a mage but close enough to seem almost like one, it's because both frequencies have intersected at a place that's not quite the middle for either of them. The world of the two have warped slightly out of shape to better accommodate one or the other.<br /> <br /> To put it in perspective, say our universe defaults at frequency 1.0, and the ChroD universe defaults at frequency 2.0. 2.0 is the world of The Vigil, where a hodge podge of movie monsters all manipulate the world, and Primordial is 2.1, where all the various creatures co-exist in their default forms and the frequency wildly fluctuates. Requiem, which resembles our world closely but also has a secret society of blood suckers, sits about 1.5; and Descent, largely detached from the going-ons of the other supernaturals and prescribing to a cosmology far removed from the real world, might sit at 2.6. If a group of hunters in Baltimore is dealing with a secret society of kindred that resemble the ideological and political split of the Requiem universe, that region of Vigil-Prime might curve towards 1.54, then snap back to its default setting once they become a tangential issue. It also means there are spaces between these universes where every individual tabletop game and homebrew setting can comfortably sit.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, on a re-read, it looks like our ideas are pretty much the same. My bad!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-23-2016, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:07:40-07:00","id":992134,"title":"","content":"This idea sounds really cool. I hope it works well for you. <br /> <br /> For my idea, I've just taken a simple answer. The God-Machine is the main system, with the other Game-Lines being separate apps within the system, run sometimes by different brands of angels, each tasked over a specific kind of supernatural. Like, for instance, The Beast being the Angel for Vampires, and Geists being angels for Soul Eaters. Basically, any higher up supernatural is an angel, and the various supernaturals are various types of Stigmatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:22:38-07:00","id":992143,"title":"","content":"Also, the Mage frequency should basically be The Venture Brothers: The World. Or The World Of Trippy Dark Mystery or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:15:44-07:00","id":992236,"title":"","content":"The only reference I didn't get was the I.C who signed the letter, and that's bothering me... can someone shed some light?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:49:43-07:00","id":992249,"title":"","content":"I'll explain it in PM if you want, but think of it this way: what's a setting somewhat similar to ChroD that has a group of massively powerful beings with the initials I.C.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:54:37-07:00","id":992255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992143#post992143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Mage frequency should basically be The Venture Brothers: The World. Or The World Of Dark Heroes or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Goddamn, I would love to put together a Venture Bros. tabletop game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:57:53-07:00","id":992257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992255#post992255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Goddamn, I would love to put together a Venture Bros. tabletop game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. As it stands, though, Genius would probably be the best fit in ChroD (as much of a pain as the mechanics are). Ascension could probably do it pretty well, but it might be best to look at one of the superhero or pulp influenced tabletop RPGs, like Spirit of the Century. <br /> <br /> ChroD and Unknown Armies are both good in that they have the systems necessary to model how psychologically broken everyone in VB is, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T22:00:20-07:00","id":992258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992257#post992257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same. As it stands, though, Genius would probably be the best fit in ChroD (as much of a pain as the mechanics are). Ascension could probably do it pretty well, but it might be best to look at one of the superhero or pulp influenced tabletop RPGs, like Spirit of the Century.<br /> <br /> ChroD and Unknown Armies are both good in that they have the systems necessary to model how psychologically broken everyone in VB is, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But can they simulate the comedy of it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd definitely make Anxieties or Insecurities a core aspect of the game model, similar to Ambitions in ChroD, but more prone to an ST using it to sabotage your successes. Create a system where succeeding in the field <i>where you really want to make it </i>is an almost insurmountable obstacle.<br /> <br /> Or maybe give it a party game vibe where everyone's Insecurities are out on the table, and any one player can snatch the card up and use it to twist the results of another player's rolls.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think what you'd have to do is build a system established from the ground up around those concepts of failure, probably with a very stripped down mechanical system (using only core attributes and field specializations, perhaps?). You give your character a Crippling Insecurity that comes into play and always activates whenever the right criteria are met (like a tilt or condition in ChroD terms): faint in the presence of pretty women, never live up to your father's legacy, never fail to indulge a vice. The kind of things that can always show up at random and throw a monkey wrench in even your most orchestrated plans. Then set up a Failed Ambition (become the world's greatest super scientist or kill Doctor Venture, for instance), and say, four failures you've suffered in your past attempts to reach that. You can never pass up an opportunity to achieve your Ambition, but your Crippling Insecurity more or less ensures that you never succeed at it. Coming to terms in some way with your failures becomes one of your core objectives and a driving plot hook, and as you resolve them, you have the opportunity to replace them with healthier and more achievable objectives.<br /> <br /> Also everyone gets to build their Arch. Maybe you take a troupe approach to storytelling, similar to the Shadows system of Wraith: The Oblivion, where everyone plays their own character and someone else's Arch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-24-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T23:14:19-07:00","id":992272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992071#post992071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! Mind if I steal the basic naming scheme?<br /> <br /> So, here's how it's set up, with nine worlds::<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness<br /> <br /> The World of Blood<br /> <br /> The World of Spirits<br /> <br /> The World of Mana<br /> <br /> The World of Thorns<br /> <br /> The World of Fire<br /> <br /> The World of Ghosts<br /> <br /> The World of Pillars<br /> <br /> The World of Gears</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nine worlds, uh? Like in Yggdrassil, the tree of worlds? Maybe we can make parallels. Basic World of Darkness ougth to be Midgard, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:28:32-07:00","id":992416,"title":"","content":"Sorry about veering off of the original topic.<br /> <br /> I think the God-Machine could make an interesting cross-universe element here.Say the fundamental structure of every universe is girded by the cogs and gears of the machine, but in most universes, the God itself lies dormant or only peripherally effects the lives of those in it. Are these deist universes that the Machine created and has left to their own devices, or are they experimental realities designed for observation? Or is it a sort of antibody produced by the multiverse, filling in the gaps uncovered by the various worlds' mystical architecture and creating a unifying element for all the threads connecting this &quot;family&quot; or intertwined universes?<br /> <br /> Perhaps more interestingly, what does that say about the Descent universe? In a world where there's no &quot;authentic&quot; mystical force underpinning the universe, is the God-Machine forced to construct one for the sake of the world's survival? Perhaps the Descent universe serves as an anchor, preventing intrusions from dimensions outside of the conventional Chronicles of Darkness worlds. Descent-Prime perhaps as the border guard that prevents the CWoD from bleeding over into the ChroD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-24-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:56:05-07:00","id":992479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992416#post992416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps more interestingly, what does that say about the Descent universe? In a world where there's no &quot;authentic&quot; mystical force underpinning the universe, is the God-Machine forced to construct one for the sake of the world's survival? Perhaps the Descent universe serves as an anchor, preventing intrusions from dimensions outside of the conventional Chronicles of Darkness worlds. Descent-Prime perhaps as the border guard that prevents the CWoD from bleeding over into the ChroD?</div> </div> </div> </div>And if we consider translation guides as valid branches, it isn't exactly doing a bang-up job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:17:53-07:00","id":992491,"title":"","content":"Whatever take we go with, I'd personally have the Machine be out of focus except in the &quot;base&quot; world and the Demon world, as an explanation for how the other splats don't run into it more often. For example, if Mages existed in the world described in the GMC and Demon, it would be kind of hard to explain why they aren't constantly running into it (given their whole occult mystery deal). If the Machine exists on a different layer of reality for them, it would explain why it isn't more of a thing for them while also allowing them to occasionally run across it.<br /> <br /> Another idea: the names of each splat exist, but refer to more isolated phenomena outside of their own world. For example, Mage specifically means supernally connected humans in the World of Mana, but in the other worlds it's used for any human magic practitioner and is more of a general umbrella term for various minor templates and sorcerers. Someone from one of those worlds might intersect with a Mage from the World of Mana and perceive them as simply another kind of sorcerer, unless they had prolonged enough contact or discussion to anchor each other in their realities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:50:48-07:00","id":992516,"title":"","content":"I think more than a few Mages would probably have an aneurysm if this was true.<br /> <br /> Though, where would Deviant fit in this? Would they get their own world like the other major line? Or would they kind of be weird living intersections between shards and universe, due to their sheer diversity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:56:02-07:00","id":992518,"title":"","content":"I theorized that they exist in the &quot;base&quot; world and can intersect with the others, and can theoretically be created within them. <br /> <br /> And yeah, it gives Mages headaches, since they're one of the groups most likely to stumble onto it. What really gives them headaches, though, is how durable the system seems to be. It seems to only permit small-scale changes, and the borders seem to solidify when someone risks disrupting it. Take the poor Mage who set out to play vampire hunter after his test subjects kept getting stolen by the Ordo Dracul. No matter how many vampires he found, there were always more, and he could never seem to find or wipe out the governing bodies or political entities they claimed existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:50:32-07:00","id":992540,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I think this mirrors the thought pattern I had behind my own Crossover City suggestion/thread, though obviously expanded beyond the constraints of one locale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:02:54-07:00","id":992543,"title":"","content":"Also, it technically doesn't contradict canon in any way, since it's basically meant to take the state of the ChroD universe from an out of universe perspective (separate settings inside one meta-setting that occasionally intersect) and find a way to make it true from an in-universe perspective.<br /> <br /> For example, part of it is to provide a way that Mages and the God-Machine can exist in the same setting while having relatively little interaction with each other. <br /> <br /> The &quot;crossover mangrove&quot; is sort of the reverse, being an out of universe perspective on an in universe truth, that the supernatural tends to be somewhat subjective and shaped a lot by collective perception. So, for example, this theory allows that a Mage could learn about Changeling Arcadia, come to any of the many theories that have been established as to their connection, and have any of them be true, as they form as a metaphysical connecting device that allows the Mage to exist in both worlds. <br /> <br /> In a similar way to how Mages can manifest in other worlds as an umbrella for any sort of mortal magician, Horrors can potentially be any of the kinds of creature from the other worlds, but they are rarely put under the kind of magical scrutiny in the base world that could firmly establish if they are, say, a Hobgoblin or a Spirit or a Stigmatic Cryptid. Generally, intense magical scrutiny is the best mechanism of collapsing the wave function of ambiguity and creating a bridge between two reality layers. However, in some cases, ambiguity still remains due to the perception factor. A Mage could encounter the Hedge and become connected to the World of Thorns, believe it to be an Emanation Realm, or believe Hobs to be Supernal beings created by this emanation, and they could be entirely right regardless of whether or not that's the &quot;actual&quot; explanation, because their perception of them is close enough to the truth that it forms a valid reality bridge. On the flip side, a Demon might perceive a Mage as an unusually powerful Stigmatic &quot;hacking&quot; the Machine, and this would be &quot;true&quot; from the perspective of the Demon layer, just as the Mage's perception of the Machine as an aggregate of control symbols created by the Fall would be true on their side. <br /> <br /> And the reason why magic powers that depend on certain supernatural forces that may not be present in every layer work in every layer is because a person caught between two layers does not actually travel to another place but projects themself onto it, or becomes a metaphysical anchor subject to the &quot;rules&quot; of both. So a Mage's magic works even on a layer with no Supernal realms, because the Mage is still based in the World of Mana no matter what other layers they become connected to. This is where crossover theories come into play: people caught between layers must establish one to anchor themselves in place and not slide back completely into their own layers, and the bridge formed by a crossover theory permits magical phenomena from one layer to effect others. <br /> <br /> Also, the beauty of this system is that it requires no rules and mechanical changes and basically means that reality itself follows the tips from crossovers written in the books.<br /> <br /> Another idea- the Astral permeates and connects all the layers. This is why Beasts are connected to other monsters: because they are born from one of the few supernatural phenomena that is naturally equally tied to each world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:04:23-07:00","id":992562,"title":"","content":"Alright, Gecko, I don't usually hold much serious interest in your headcanon stuff, but this is some real good stuff here. I might crib this for a game at some point.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Also, this could be a really good way to integrate the Old World of Darkness without utterly destroying either setting. It lets, say, Fallen Demons remain separate from Unchained Demons but still coexist with them, and it lets the &quot;Objective Truth So Suck It&quot; Mages jive with &quot;Subjective Reality So Suck It&quot; Mages without needing to make one cosmology subservient to the other, because it's just two alternate realities with different rules intersecting briefly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 10-24-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:24:58-07:00","id":992570,"title":"","content":"Well, glad you like this one! <br /> <br /> And yeah, the other cluster I mentioned in the first post was meant to be the Old World of Darkness, and the one they tried to contact is Unknown Armies. I actually drew a &quot;map&quot; of the multiverse, with the ChroD cluster in the middle, and several others off in the distance. My idea is that the distance between a universe cluster depends on thematic and content differences. So ChroD is fairly close to UA, and close enough to oWoD that there are &quot;lines&quot; connecting them that could allow them to intersect. The oWoD cluster, additionally, has faint lines connecting it to the Exalted cluster, while both worlds of darkness are in the same multiversal &quot;neighborhood&quot; as the Anne Rice cluster, the creepypasta cluster, the Call of Cthulhu cluster, and so on. And if you were in the Unknown Armies cluster, you'd have an easier time getting to the Illuminatus Trilogy cluster or the Tim Powers cluster than you would getting to the Star Wars cluster. <br /> <br /> I'd personally not have the oWoD universes be part of the ChroD layer knot, but that's how canon works- you pick which one you want. I already assume that Mage and Promethean as they exist in my universe knot are different from the way they exist in other peoples' universe knots, for example, because there are no actual universe knots and all of this exists solely in our minds. <br /> <br /> To establish some terminology, I'm thinking each layer has its own Paradigm (dominant supernatural methodology) and Primacy (powerful background supernatural string-pullers). Example Paradigms would be the Spirit World, the Supernal, the Wyrd, the Divine Fire, and so on, while Primacies would be super powerful spirits, Exarchs and other Supernal beings, the Gentry, the Principle, the Judges, and Machine, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:13:15-07:00","id":992869,"title":"","content":"The God Machine is a good story, but I would not only &quot;eliminate&quot; it from other worlds, I wouldn't have it not even in the Base World, either. That's because my personal take on the base world is that absolutely nothing can be tied to a higher explanation. It is the World of Mystery. Instead, the World of Gears is similar enough to the World of Darkness that playing a mortal character isn't all that different, and you can have a similar experience.<br /> <br /> By the way, one of the things to keep in mind is that some phenomena, like humanity, isn't exclusive to a given world. Hunters and mystery finders of every kind can exist in all worlds, and that will make a Mortals game have a distinct flavor depending on the world it mostly happens. I am specialy fond of mortal games in the CoD, mind you.<br /> <br /> I have to agree that this thread is really, really good stuff to work. And I'll put it to use soon enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:52:43-07:00","id":993177,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth noting that the original World of Darkness included something very much like this, both in <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> (where it mentioned that the World of Darkness used to be composed of multiple layers of reality tightly coupled together, with each representing a different take on matters) and in the Time of Judgment supplement <b>Mage</b> (where it was referred to as the Fractured Cosmos, and posited a similar scenario but with much looser bindings between the different variants of reality). <br /> <br /> It's something I like where the original World of Darkness is concerned, as the various gamelines had metaphysics that sometimes clashed violently (though it's possible that One World of Darkness will address this issue). I'm not so fond of using it with the Chronicles of Darkness, because by and large most gamelines don't have or need dominance of their paradigms: for instance, the Divine Fire, animism, and the Wyrd all coexist without any of them being the ultimate underpinnings of reality. The Supernal is the only exception to this, and even it isn't so much a dominant paradigm that everything else is subservient to as it's the index of reality: e.g., it isn't that the Wyrd is a manifestation of the Supernal as it is that the Supernal describes the Wyrd. Without the various metaphysics competing with each other for the role of dominant paradigm, there are no clashes between them in need of resolution. The main exception to this is <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b>, which as written allows mortals to do things that other gamelines consider to be impossible. I don't know if that will still be true once HtV2e comes out, though. <br /> <br /> In fact, I suspect that a major motivation behind the upcoming Crossover Chronicles will be to identify apparent clashes between the lines and iron them out so that you <i>can</i> have a single, consistent ChroD setting that includes every gameline. <br /> <br /> That said, I <i>do</i> use something like this for the Chronicles of Darkness: but rather than the dividing line being gameline-based, I have it based on ChroD's toolbox nature. That is, you have a single ChroD &quot;core reality&quot;, and then a bunch of customized variants emanating out from it, each corresponding to a particular Storyteller's take on the ChroD. For instance, my default ChroD setting doesn't have vampires or Beasts in it, because I have little interest in either of those gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:20:47-07:00","id":993184,"title":"","content":"I've kind of adjusted myself to two ChroDs- one where there's everything except the Supernal, and &quot;mage&quot; is a blanket term for any kind of mortal who performs occult practices, and one, which I'm currently working on, where the Supernal exists and lies at the root of all supernatural abilities, and the entire cosmology and universe revolve around the story of their Awakened and their battle for reality. Elements from the other splats exist as elements of the Mage cosmology. For example, the True Fae are explicitly Fate entities solidified from Supernal Arcadia. The major splats except Mage exist in some way as Merits or Legacies. So, a Mage could be a highly advanced homunculus or other artificial being, or a Changeling. And the Uratha and Sin-Eaters are legacies. Basically, ChroD-1 is where I can have my own self-indulgent HORROR! MONSTERS! thematic purity festival, and ChroD-M is where I can go wild with Mage without worrying I'm trespassing on the ground of other splats. I fully acknowledge this is entirely my own personal hang-up, but I still like this way of handling things. <br /> <br /> I actually really like making alternate universe versions of my characters, and this gives me yet another way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:53:32-07:00","id":993196,"title":"","content":"That's the beauty of Shards: you can do whatever you want with them.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm trying to say is that your model strikes me as overcomplicated. Given the efforts being made to keep the Chronicles of Darkness games consistent with each other, I don't see much need for anything more elaborate than a single core world (representing the setting that the publisher has in mind) surrounded by a cloud of Shards, each tailored by a given gaming group to suit their preferences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-25-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:02:07-07:00","id":993203,"title":"","content":"So, the mangrove model seems overly complicated? To be honest, I pretty much gave it up once I came up with splitting ChroD and Mage. <br /> <br /> Also, let's face it, if Mages as they're described exist in the same world of the Machine, as its described, they'd be constantly falling ass forwards into Infrastructure, and there's no real way to get around that other than storytelling fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:28:39-07:00","id":993215,"title":"","content":"Hey; if that duality works for you, have fun with it. I don't see much common ground between your Mage-based Shard and Mage 2e; but that's merely a reason why <i>I</i> wouldn't use your setup. <br /> <br /> As for mages stumbling over the GM: mages stumble over <i>everyone</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:42:32-07:00","id":993224,"title":"","content":"This is off topic, and if you have suggestions we should probably take this to my thread for discussing the hack. I should note that I'm not going with a lot of the changes I had planned for The Hollow Chronicle, and I'm not going for the whole &quot;all mages are inherently broken monsters!!!&quot; thing I was pushing before. <br /> <br /> The project, as it is, isn't about restricting Mage the way my old attempt to awkwardly shove it into the whole of my needlessly nitpicky expectations, it's about taking Mage 2e as it is, celebrating that, and incorporating elements from the other lines into it in ways specifically meant to enhance the experience of people playing Mages. <br /> <br /> I'm accepting that my reasons for convincing myself that I didn't like Mage were entirely due to my own biases and obsessions, and that what I was trying to do really was a bad idea: making a new game, or making Mage completely different in a quixotic quest for my own narrow perception thematic purity, isn't eventually going to get things anywhere. <br /> <br /> I guess this isn't so much a hack as a set of homebrew- some new legacies and adaptations of stuff from other lines to Mage cosmology.<br /> <br /> And come on, that's a cop-out. If Mages and the Machine existed in the same world, both as they're describes, then each would be a primary antagonistic force for the other. I'm not saying that you can't cross them over, or do stuff with that, or adjust the scope and particulars of either, but I personally prefer having the Machine as the great occult power of one universe, and the Supernal as the magical center of another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-25-2016, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:53:04-07:00","id":993230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=993224#post993224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And come on, that's a cop-out. If Mages and the Machine existed in the same world, both as they're describes, then each would be a primary antagonistic force for the other. I'm not saying that you can't cross them over, or do stuff with that, or adjust the scope and particulars of either, but I personally prefer having the Machine as the great occult power of one universe, and the Supernal as the magical center of another.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Machine has had since before recorded history to learn how to avoid notice, to the point where the only things that can really find it reliably are <i>things that used to be it</i>. It's not that Mages are oblivious, so much as that the God-Machine is an alien intelligence that's existed for longer than anyone and has had to deal with nosy dicks like them for basically all of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:42:41-07:00","id":993311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=993230#post993230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the Machine has had since before recorded history to learn how to avoid notice, to the point where the only things that can really find it reliably are <i>things that used to be it</i>. It's not that Mages are oblivious, so much as that the God-Machine is an alien intelligence that's existed for longer than anyone and has had to deal with nosy dicks like them for basically all of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the vast majority of its activities operate under the auspices of the specific category of supernatural effect that explicitly doesn't ping Peripheral Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Demons having blanket immunity to the mystical effects of Concealment Infrastructure doesn't mean the Awakened make a beeline for every project under God's gray Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:04:38-07:00","id":993338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992869#post992869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine is a good story, but I would not only &quot;eliminate&quot; it from other worlds, I wouldn't have it not even in the Base World, either. That's because my personal take on the base world is that absolutely nothing can be tied to a higher explanation. It is the World of Mystery. Instead, the World of Gears is similar enough to the World of Darkness that playing a mortal character isn't all that different, and you can have a similar experience.<br /> <br /> By the way, one of the things to keep in mind is that some phenomena, like humanity, isn't exclusive to a given world. Hunters and mystery finders of every kind can exist in all worlds, and that will make a Mortals game have a distinct flavor depending on the world it mostly happens. I am specialy fond of mortal games in the CoD, mind you.<br /> <br /> I have to agree that this thread is really, really good stuff to work. And I'll put it to use soon enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, I'd take the opposite route, just because if I'm going to have this unified cosmology, I want there to be hooks there tying everything together. For me, the God-Machine is an interesting mythology that doesn't need to be obtrusive but can create a creeping sense of interconnectivity and make this idea of a multiverse a centerpiece for a Demon game in this setting.<br /> <br /> I look at it like this. At the highest frequency, you have the World of Gears, where the God-Machine is an omnipresent force. It's all about Demons vs. infrastructure. The implication being that the G-M is a sort of safeguard protecting the ChroD superstructure from incursions from higher planes. It adds some selfishness and ambiguity to the agenda of demons trying to tear it down.<br /> <br /> Drop down a level and you have the Mageverse, where the G-M isn't really present, but the remnants of it are still hidden away. Mages occasionally stumble upon these elaborate, enigmatic gears at the center of the universe, but whatever used to turn them seems dormant or dead, and no one has been able to wrap their head around the puzzle of how this machinery functions.<br /> <br /> Drop all the way down to Mortalworld, and all you hear is hints and rumors. You might hear madmen rambling about the cogs that keep the multiverse turning, but they never amount to much, and there's nothing to substantiate their elaborate mandalas and their crazed diatribes. Implication being that they crossed over to this higher frequency and were irrevocably altered by it.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd probably sprinkle these hints of other universes throughout the lines. A werewolf pack stumbles upon a secret ledger outlining the secret power plays of a society called the Invictus, but they can't find any evidence that it ever existed. A mage has vivid, recurring dreams in which they're trapped in a place called the Hedge. They're practically waking nightmares, and it feels as if these fantasies are something they legitimately lived, but their studies lead them consistently to nothing but dead ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-26-2016, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:19:18-07:00","id":993345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=992491#post992491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea: the names of each splat exist, but refer to more isolated phenomena outside of their own world. For example, Mage specifically means supernally connected humans in the World of Mana, but in the other worlds it's used for any human magic practitioner and is more of a general umbrella term for various minor templates and sorcerers. Someone from one of those worlds might intersect with a Mage from the World of Mana and perceive them as simply another kind of sorcerer, unless they had prolonged enough contact or discussion to anchor each other in their realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that there are minor templates of other supernaturals in the various worlds? In Hunter-Prime we have a hodge podge of all the core beasties that resemble but aren't the same as the core book splats, and there are various breeds of sorcerers that reflect the cosmologies of the different universes.<br /> <br /> Are there werewolves in Requiemworld? Not Uratha, but rare monstrosities that reflect an externalized perspective of the kindreds' internal struggle with the beast? Are there vampires in the World of Mana? Not kindred, but blighted parasitic creatures that have made infernal pacts with otherworldly creatures? Do Death-Talkers prowl the fringes of the Forsaken World?<br /> <br /> Maybe all of these universes intrinsically want to knit themselves together in a shape that resembles the larger tapestry, most fully realized in the Beast Universe and almost achieved in the Hunterverse. But the Forsaken World can't fully replicate the shape that vampires, prometheans, mages, etc. <i>should </i>take without contradicting their inherent mythology, so by necessity they have to create these half-formed things that fit more comfortably within the dominant paradigm. The Forsaken World knows that there <i>should</i> be vampires. After all, just one block over there's a sister universe in which they infest the streets of every major city and have their own complex society; but it can't sustain that sort of complex infrastructure, so it cobbles together its own version of vampires that fits more organically within its spirit-dominant ecosystem. The World of Mana is one phase shift away from the Descentverse. It knows that a God-Machine <i>should </i>exist, so remnants of it <i>do </i>exist. But it's not the God-Machine. Not really. It's just the scattered remnants of a long dead civilization that shouldn't and maybe never did exist. Sometimes these worlds cross over, and that means a mage briefly stumbles into the World of Spirits, but there's an even more distinct imact from this bleeding effect. Remnants of these other universes rub off on one another and become filtered through that world's paradigm into something new. It's multiversal debris left stranded in a world it shouldn't belong, mutated by that universe's inherent need for assimilation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-26-2016, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:43:50-07:00","id":993352,"title":"","content":"The answer to all of your questions is:<br /> <br /> I am very very lazy and am not going to develop this idea further, and even if I did it wouldn't matter because the answer is literally always whatever would be the most interesting for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:50:10-07:00","id":993355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=993352#post993352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer to all of your questions is:<br /> <br /> I am very very lazy and am not going to develop this idea further, and even if I did it wouldn't matter because the answer is literally always whatever would be the most interesting for you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I wasn't genuinely looking for you to expand or integrate ideas into your homebrew. I just like speculating about the metaphysics of fictional worlds. Think of the questions as rhetorical. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:18:06-07:00","id":993793,"title":"","content":"What I found interesting in the Mangrove Model, mind you, isn't the idea of using the model as cosmology of Shards, but the Model as an example of how some clusters of Shards can [i]interact[/u]. What comes from the contact between realities is as important as the realities themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=993338#post993338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I'd take the opposite route, just because if I'm going to have this unified cosmology, I want there to be hooks there tying everything together. For me, the God-Machine is an interesting mythology that doesn't need to be obtrusive but can create a creeping sense of interconnectivity and make this idea of a multiverse a centerpiece for a Demon game in this setting.<br /> <br /> I look at it like this. At the highest frequency, you have the World of Gears, where the God-Machine is an omnipresent force. It's all about Demons vs. infrastructure. The implication being that the G-M is a sort of safeguard protecting the ChroD superstructure from incursions from higher planes. It adds some selfishness and ambiguity to the agenda of demons trying to tear it down.<br /> <br /> Drop down a level and you have the Mageverse, where the G-M isn't really present, but the remnants of it are still hidden away. Mages occasionally stumble upon these elaborate, enigmatic gears at the center of the universe, but whatever used to turn them seems dormant or dead, and no one has been able to wrap their head around the puzzle of how this machinery functions.<br /> <br /> Drop all the way down to Mortalworld, and all you hear is hints and rumors. You might hear madmen rambling about the cogs that keep the multiverse turning, but they never amount to much, and there's nothing to substantiate their elaborate mandalas and their crazed diatribes. Implication being that they crossed over to this higher frequency and were irrevocably altered by it.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd probably sprinkle these hints of other universes throughout the lines. A werewolf pack stumbles upon a secret ledger outlining the secret power plays of a society called the Invictus, but they can't find any evidence that it ever existed. A mage has vivid, recurring dreams in which they're trapped in a place called the Hedge. They're practically waking nightmares, and it feels as if these fantasies are something they legitimately lived, but their studies lead them consistently to nothing but dead ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a matter of what you want from the setting, and that's why I prefer to not make such assumption at first. To begin you need only to define what happens usually and what can be detected at some frequency. You don't need to define at this level what causes any of this, let that be defined by the needs of the specific chronicle.<br /> <br /> That said, you can use a lot of different things as the ultimate link between the worlds of the cluster. Maybe truth hides in the deeps of the Shadow, under the control of some infinitely mighty spirit. Or in the deeps of the Underworld, where the secrets of creation literally lie dead at the nadir of creation. Or in the farthest reaches of Arcadia, where the source of all stories lie.<br /> <br /> But when you predefine things, you kill ideas in the crib. Of course, it is all sound and good if you and your PCs like the God Machine enough to want it as the final mystery every time. As some people will want the Archmages or the Exarchs as such.<br /> <br /> All that aside, the speculations are good fodder for ever new clusters and universes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:36:39-07:00","id":993864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=993793#post993793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I found interesting in the Mangrove Model, mind you, isn't the idea of using the model as cosmology of Shards, but the Model as an example of how some clusters of Shards can [i]interact[/u]. What comes from the contact between realities is as important as the realities themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its a matter of what you want from the setting, and that's why I prefer to not make such assumption at first. To begin you need only to define what happens usually and what can be detected at some frequency. You don't need to define at this level what causes any of this, let that be defined by the needs of the specific chronicle.<br /> <br /> That said, you can use a lot of different things as the ultimate link between the worlds of the cluster. Maybe truth hides in the deeps of the Shadow, under the control of some infinitely mighty spirit. Or in the deeps of the Underworld, where the secrets of creation literally lie dead at the nadir of creation. Or in the farthest reaches of Arcadia, where the source of all stories lie.<br /> <br /> But when you predefine things, you kill ideas in the crib. Of course, it is all sound and good if you and your PCs like the God Machine enough to want it as the final mystery every time. As some people will want the Archmages or the Exarchs as such.<br /> <br /> All that aside, the speculations are good fodder for ever new clusters and universes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you may misunderstand. I'm not talking about this as any sort of personal canon. More just talking about what could make for interesting hypothetical settings. The G-M example was more just an example of how these various mythologies echo through the frequencies rather than as some grand unifying strand in the multiverse.<br /> <br /> It's more just background flavor. I mean, I suppose the decaying and rusted bones of a God-Machine could make a cool set piece for a Mage game, but otherwise, it's not a present enough entity to work as a central story element outside of Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T04:07:04-07:00","id":993972,"title":"","content":"Well, I would excise the assumption that the God-Machine have any specific function or place in the cosmology (except for the Gear World). But the way you describe it isn't bad. At most I'm not sure if those worlds are set in any specific order to make some &quot;next in the line&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't have too much time now to address that, but someone could find similar descriptions of how hints of the Powers that Be from the other worlds bleed in cluster.<br /> <br /> I have to add, as a personal note and not saying that your post in particular did such a thing, that I'm a bit tired of G-M and Mage fans posting here and there as if their cosmologies were the ultimate answer to everything, and not just an option. It isn't entirely wrong, since they <u>are</u> options, nor have I something against the people doing it, but the frequent &quot;G-M would never be caught that way&quot; vs &quot;An Archmage would watch this and laugh&quot; is becoming quite annoying by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T09:23:48-07:00","id":994062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992054-cofd-cosmology-idea-linked-universes?p=993972#post993972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to add, as a personal note and not saying that your post in particular did such a thing, that I'm a bit tired of G-M and Mage fans posting here and there as if their cosmologies were the ultimate answer to everything, and not just an option. It isn't entirely wrong, since they <u>are</u> options, nor have I something against the people doing it, but the frequent &quot;G-M would never be caught that way&quot; vs &quot;An Archmage would watch this and laugh&quot; is becoming quite annoying by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm a bit more interested in how the Vampire Elders and the Covenants would react to finding about other universes. I'm pretty sure that this thread is going with the idea that a few individuals step into the wrong frequency, but vampires tend to surprisingly gossip a lot for such a secretive society. I'm wondering how Ordo Dracul Elders would react to the idea of these different frequencies, or how Priests of the Lancea et Sanctum would try to incorporate such ideas into their faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:07:54-07:00","id":994258,"title":"","content":"Gossip and secrecy walk together a lot even in real life, they feed one another. People gossip because there are so much secrets to talk about, and people keep secrets under ever more layers of secrecy because they're under so much scrutiny.<br /> <br /> I think the Ordo Dracul would take a great interest in those other-worlds. Places and ways to access them, even partially, would be charted. The Ordo would try to control and profit from intrusions from other places, and organize expeditions out there. On most cities, they would be the only ones in the know of such phenomena. Probably the other Covenants would take a less default view on the matter, and be very little affected on their world view. If a god can create a world, it can create as many as it want. The specific Kindred involved and the specific links would have a great deal of impact on their stance, while we can draw something more clearly for the Ordo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T19:16:16-07:00","id":994340,"title":"","content":"Hm, that is a fair point. There isn't as much incentive for vampires to find out about that stuff, is there. Except for the Ordo of course, seeing as that is kind of their bag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}